WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.720
Tesla may have six factories around the world. 
 &nbsp;

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.720
But none is more important than its&nbsp;
mega factory near Austin, Texas. 
 &nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.640
This building is the most advanced car&nbsp;
factory that earth has ever seen 
 
 &nbsp;

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.000
If you could put the building on its side,&nbsp;
Tesla’s new headquarters would be taller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.760
than the world’s tallest skyscrapers,&nbsp;
including Dubai’s Burj Khalifa. 
 &nbsp;

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.920
According to our calculations, you can fit&nbsp;
194 billion hamsters in this building! 
 &nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.480
Billions of hamsters and one day millions of&nbsp;
cars are expected to roll off the assembly line.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.800
For the past twenty years, Tesla has been&nbsp;
following its carefully concocted plan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.880
to ‘electrify’ the world. 
 
In 2006, Elon musk released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:44.000
Tesla’s Master Plan Part 1, on its website. 
 
It consisted of, first, “building a sports&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.840
car” - the Roadster. It was really expensive,&nbsp;
with a starting price of over $100,000,
 &nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.640
Second, “Using that money to build an affordable&nbsp;
car” - the Model S and X - though both are pricey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.480
and still out of the reach of most.
 
Third: “Use that money to build an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:03.360
even more affordable car” - which gave us&nbsp;
the Model 3 and the Model Y crossover. 
 &nbsp;

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:08.400
Finally, “While doing above, also provide&nbsp;
zero-emission electric power generation options”.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.920
In reference to Tesla’s solar&nbsp;
lineup of solar panels, roof tiles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.640
and powerwalls to supply energy to your home.
 &nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.960
A decade later, Tesla came out with&nbsp;
Master Plan, part Deux, or Part Two. 
 &nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.120
“Create stunning solar roofs with&nbsp;
seamlessly integrated battery storage.”

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.040
Tesla’s solar tiles have been more difficult&nbsp;
to install than originally thought because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.920
no two roofs are the same. I went into detail in&nbsp;
another video that I’ll link in my description. 
 &nbsp;

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:37.200
Second, “Expand the electric vehicle&nbsp;
product line to address all major segments”
 &nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.120
Besides the S, 3, X, and Y, Tesla’s Cybertruck&nbsp;
is FINALLY slated to go into production next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:48.320
year according to Musk after a longggg&nbsp;
wait. The semi is also in progress. 
 &nbsp;

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.320
Third, “Develop a self-driving&nbsp;
capability that is 10X safer than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.240
manual via massive fleet learning”. 
 
The software to make the Tesla fully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.160
self-driving is still being developed. 
 
Which is connected to the final point of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.880
Master Plan part 2: “Enable your car to make&nbsp;
money for you when you aren't using it.” 
 &nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:10.560
A self-driving network of cars, or robotaxis,&nbsp;
is dependent on FSD being complete. 
 &nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.680
In March, Musk confirmed he’s&nbsp;
working on Master Plan Part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:19.520
3…despite Part Two not being fully finished. 
 
However, he’s always been one to look ahead.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:23.200
Part three is likely to see electric&nbsp;
cars streaming off assembly lines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.280
at a rate never before seen.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:30.880
A scale that no company has ever&nbsp;
achieved in the history of humanity. 
 &nbsp;

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.240
Tesla’s growth has already been astounding. It’s&nbsp;
the fastest-growing car manufacturer in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:40.400
currently delivering a million cars a year. 
 
But if you know anything about Elon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.640
Musk - his appetite is bigger. 
 
If Tesla’s share of the total vehicle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:50.720
output market globally is about 1%...Musk&nbsp;
says his company is aiming for 20% of the pie.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.520
In other words, he wants 1 out of every five&nbsp;
new cars on the road to be one of his.  
 &nbsp;

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:00.400
Musk has repeatedly said developing prototypes&nbsp;
are a piece of cake compared to the complicated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.880
process of scaling up production. 
 
The only way to achieve that scale is to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.440
your factory as efficient as possible. 
 
The layout of Giga Texas is very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.440
different compared to Tesla’s original&nbsp;
headquarters in Fremont, California. 
 &nbsp;

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.680
Fremont’s factory consisted of separate&nbsp;
buildings making different parts. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.360
the seats were made in a totally different&nbsp;
building from the main assembly line.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.520
So it wasn’t as efficient as it could have been.
 &nbsp;

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:29.520
Whereas now, with Giga Texas, everything is under&nbsp;
one roof. Almost like an integrated circuit.
 &nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.280
Raw materials come in one door, and the&nbsp;
finished product goes out the other.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.960
Within the factory, Tesla is also&nbsp;
simplifying the way it makes its cars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.760
thanks to its giant casting machines known as&nbsp;
the Giga Press. The Austin-made Model Ys are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.720
produced with only two body pieces at the front&nbsp;
and rear whereas the Model 3s have 171 pieces.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:50.960
The Ys also contain 1,600 fewer welds. Fewer steps&nbsp;
on the production line translate to lower cost.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:56.480
Speaking of lowering costs, Tesla is building&nbsp;
its own battery cells in house, the 4680s.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:02.160
These next generation batteries pack more energy,&nbsp;
the company says they’ll have 16% more range.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.960
They’re totally different from&nbsp;
the batteries of the past.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:09.200
In the same way that aircraft wings store&nbsp;
fuel instead of needing a fuel tank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.640
Tesla decided to build a battery pack&nbsp;
that doesn’t contain excess structure.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.520
So, what’s next for Tesla?

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:21.200
It could truly transform into an AI company. 
 
Musk has always insisted the goal of Tesla&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:25.440
is not to be a car company but a technology&nbsp;
company that’s developing software so the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.400
cars can drive themselves. 
 
Although we thought robotaxis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:32.960
were going to look like regular Teslas,&nbsp;
Musk has alluded to a “futuristic look”.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:36.240
He said on Tesla’s first quarter of&nbsp;
earnings call that the robotaxi won’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:41.040
have a steering wheel or pedals, and the&nbsp;
company is targeting 2024 for production.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.160
If the Cybertruck is anything to go by, then&nbsp;
the robotaxi will likely turn heads as well.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:51.360
All of the tech in the Teslas is expected&nbsp;
to be packed into their robots. 
 &nbsp;

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:55.280
According to Tesla, the Optimus comes&nbsp;
complete with autopilot cameras in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:58.160
head and a full self-driving computer in the body.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:02.240
The bot is designed to take care of boring,&nbsp;
repetitive tasks that humans normally do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.680
like running to the grocery store. 
 
When Musk revealed the Tesla bot at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:09.680
the company’s AI day in 2021,&nbsp;
some thought it was a joke.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:13.440
It didn’t help that the bot was actually&nbsp;
a human dressed as a robot since there’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:16.000
not yet a prototype. 
 
But according to Musk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.480
this is no laughing matter.
 
Clip I was surprised that people did not realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:27.520
the magnitude of the Optimus robot program.&nbsp;
Those who are insightful or listen carefully will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:34.560
understand that Optimus ultimately will be worth&nbsp;
more than the car business. Worth more than FSD. 
 &nbsp;

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:39.760
The labor market is reported to be&nbsp;
16 times greater than the car market.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.640
If Tesla produces a robot that can do what we do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:46.240
this could reshape what we do with&nbsp;
our time beyond our imagination. 
 
 &nbsp;

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:51.200
Tesla started out twenty years ago as a&nbsp;
company trying to build an electric car. 
 &nbsp;

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.040
Now it’s trying to develop cars that&nbsp;
will one day drive themselves. 
 &nbsp;

00:05:55.040 --> 00:06:00.480
And if it accomplishes that, it will transform&nbsp;
into an AI company with an army of robotaxis and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:05.840
robots, and a full clean energy suite that&nbsp;
is all tied together in one neat package.

